                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d2ccc8a-d7b5-35c7-830a-c8cc5ad56396",
                                        "entry_id": "fc178c07-4c3f-330f-ab71-59407a884ff3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A split or separation within a group or organization, typically caused by discord."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5e27c7c-485e-4b46-9d6a-7523390e08d8",
                                                "sense_id": "6d2ccc8a-d7b5-35c7-830a-c8cc5ad56396",
                                                "text": "Despite personal schisms and differences in spiritual experience, there is a very coherent theology of Snape shared between the wives. To examine this manifestation of religious fandom, I will first discuss the canon scepticism and anti-Rowling sentiment that helps to contextualise the wider belief in Snape as a character who extends beyond book and film."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d60733a-b691-45a5-8028-66e195cedc96",
                                                "sense_id": "6d2ccc8a-d7b5-35c7-830a-c8cc5ad56396",
                                                "text": "But Harry, in his civilian suit, was also a reminder of the schism between the traditional and the modern in the royal family that can’t be drowned out by pageantry."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f247e58f-8858-3bb3-94ad-90e55d1fe574",
                                        "entry_id": "fc178c07-4c3f-330f-ab71-59407a884ff3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A formal division or split within a religious body."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08b13dc4-fd4a-40da-85cf-c1de1719549a",
                                                "sense_id": "f247e58f-8858-3bb3-94ad-90e55d1fe574",
                                                "text": "The schism between Sunnis and Shias happened quite early in Islamic history."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d97cc5ed-825d-3722-961c-d6e72ec792d2",
                                        "entry_id": "fc178c07-4c3f-330f-ab71-59407a884ff3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "a split within Christianity whereby a group no longer recognizes the Bishop of Rome as the head of the Church, but shares essentially the same beliefs with the Church of Rome. In other words, a political split without the introduction of heresy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "schism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1143a15-1620-3b37-a8a5-45497071ef44",
                                        "entry_id": "3790dfef-4716-37e8-b979-79f7912c9b7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To split, divide (a group or organization)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "993d3436-67a0-40c1-9e45-caa511bd6080",
                                                "sense_id": "d1143a15-1620-3b37-a8a5-45497071ef44",
                                                "text": "“This is going to schism Maga terribly online,” Kirk said. “You're going to see—I don't want to say a Maga civil war, but it's going to be a Maga online food fight that is going to be very hard to navigate.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
